00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.993
And she's going to take that information

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:46.828
and use that to build a trial date.

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:48.162
Now, I know one of the defense attorneys,

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:49.664
John Laura, has been saying

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:50.123
this trial

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.125
could take nine months to a year.

00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:54.294
But let's think about it for a minute.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.379
The prosecution has the burden of proof.

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:58.214
The prosecution is the whole show.

00:04:58.214 --> 00:04:59.590
They put the whole trial on.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.092
The defendant doesn't have to do a thing.

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:02.176
They don't have to open.

00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:03.219
They don't have to cross-examine

00:05:03.219 --> 00:05:03.636
a witness

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.638
they don't even have to put on a defense

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.556
